 "verdict": "CONDITIONING via optimiser-progress NOT SUPPORTED (exploratory). (1) The progress gap does NOT track performance: gap ordering (biggest->smallest) = ['Ackley8', 'Rosenbrock', 'GSobol'], but the only win is GSobol, which has the SMALLEST gap (+0.198); Rosenbrock (+0.359) and Ackley8 (+15.276) have LARGER gaps yet NO win, so optimiser progress != performance. (2) EI's optimiser does NOT fail on GSobol (frac_restarts_improved 0.999, mean log-improvement 1.306): its large gradients do not impair acqf optimisation -- EI reaches essentially the same relative acqf max as LogEI. (3) By the coarse max/median dispersion proxy GSobol is the LEAST ill-conditioned (4.1) of the three, not the most. => What is unique to GSobol is large gradient MAGNITUDE co-occurring with the LogEI win, but the proposed MECHANISM (large grads -> optimiser failure -> LogEI rescue) is not borne out; LogEI's GSobol win is NOT explained by conditioning-via-optimiser-progress and remains unexplained by this test."
